ok - a pushed open pull request keeps the item and the merge watch, and the watch fires when it later merges
ok - --force does not close a ship whose pull request is still open
ok - an open pull request with unpushed commits refuses teardown and keeps the backlog item
ok - an unreadable pull request refuses teardown, including --force and --keep-open
ok - teardown reuses its first PR classification when the forge becomes unavailable
ok - released copies stay open until merge and complete without a second removal (interrupted=0)
ok - released copies stay open until merge and complete without a second removal (interrupted=1)
ok - open Herdr children retain endpoint identity and home through unconfirmed and forced cleanup
ok - merge hold retains lifecycle serialization through cleanup
ok - merge waits preserve captain questions and hold lifecycles with and without dependents
ok - --keep-open holds an open pull request and names the items that still list it
